<newsitem itemid="94568" id="root" date="1996-10-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Reuters 52nd ex-UK air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 52nd ex-UK air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>This is Reuters' 52nd ex-UK air cargo market report.It will be published regularly until a new version is issued on October 16.</p>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK GBP air cargo market rates per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one:</p>
<p>						     Oct 3   vs   Sept 18</p>
<p>	     UNITED STATES</p>
<p>    LON-JFK					0.62	   0.61</p>
<p>    LON-LAX					0.70	   0.69</p>
<p>    LON-CHI					0.68	   0.69</p>
<p>	     ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p>    LON-HKG					1.19	   1.18</p>
<p>    LON-SIN					1.24	   1.23</p>
<p>    LON-NRT					1.97	   1.95</p>
<p>    LON-SEL					1.85	   1.83</p>
<p>    LON-SYD					2.07	   2.05</p>
<p>	     MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p>    LON-DXB					0.71	   0.70</p>
<p>    LON-BAH					0.85	   0.85</p>
<p>	     AFRICA</p>
<p>    LON-JNB					 1.70	   1.69</p>
<p>	     SCANDINAVIA</p>
<p>    LON-STO					0.71	   0.70</p>
<p>    LON-CPH					0.65	   0.65</p>
<p>	     LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p>    LON-SAO					2.06	   2.06</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity.</p>
</text>
